+# SCOUT RADAR — 2026-10-28, Sweep III (R17–R20)
+
+Complementary perimeter sweep. Radar I landed R1–R12; radar II landed R13–R16 and
+filed proposals #1647–#1650. This sweep covers four lanes both radars left open,
+all evidence-dated, all with primary-source proof fetched live this cycle through
+the scout's read-only URL reader (`github_read_external_file`) plus web
+corroboration. Zero speculative tickets: every proposal below names the federation
+surface it lands on and the first concrete step.
+
+Method note: this cycle's assigned role was `ecosystem-scout` (single-runner lock,
+cadence dispatch). The loop's high-signal doctrine (#1658) is honored literally —
+one proposal was considered and *not* filed (see "Considered and held back").
+
+## Covered lanes
+
+| # | Lane | Source | Status / date | Why it matters to the federation | Verdict |
+|---|------|--------|---------------|-----------------------------------|---------|
+| R17 | Agent Skills open standard (SKILL.md) | `agentskills/agentskills` — 26,702★, Apache-2.0 / CC-BY-4.0, spec at agentskills.io/specification; spec origin: Anthropic, released as open standard | Client roster growing; active spec evolution (discussion #392 `required-tools`, following `allowed-tools`) | The federation runs **three** coexisting skill-metadata conventions with no cross-validation (details below) | `ADOPT_IMMEDIATELY` → **#1672** |
+| R18 | chrome-devtools-mcp — Chrome DevTools as an MCP tool server | `ChromeDevTools/chrome-devtools-mcp` — 54,286★, Apache-2.0, official Google org, npm + CLI | Launched Sep–Oct 2025; actively maintained; README documents CI patterns (pinned versions, headless containers) | The repo hand-rolls the same capability in the `devtools-audit` skill; the `human-eye` role's FCP<1.0s mandate has no lab-data tooling behind it | `ADOPT_IMMEDIATELY` → **#1673** |
